{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4eb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a814-198f-7de0-9f8f-cc12fecf9427"},"sequence":208,"recorded_at":1780531400000411,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c85271b6-2806-4b59-af83-bf3e3b19854f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"c85271b6-2806-4b59-af83-bf3e3b19854f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c85271b6-2806-4b59-af83-bf3e3b19854f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a814-cf24-7cf1-8c03-9ae21e1378f7"},"task_id":"01a0a814-cf24-7cf1-8c03-9ae21e1378f7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a814-cf24-7cf1-8c03-9ae21e1378f7","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/.agents/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md`.\n1|# Resources\n2|\n3|Resources are owned by the board element they are attached to. Use explicit\n4|CRUD operations against that element ID. Local payloads are grouped under\n5|`.task-board/.resources/<elementID>/`; remote board-server uses the equivalent\n6|element-scoped filesystem or MinIO object-key prefix.\n7|\n8|## Resource Types\n9|\n10|| Type | Purpose | Example |\n11||------|---------|---------|\n12|| **precondition** | Inputs needed before work starts | Design docs, specs, instructions, API schemas |\n13|| **outcome** | Results produced by work | Research findings, implementation notes, analysis |\n14|\n15|## Commands\n16|\n17|```bash\n18|# Create a resource\n19|task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=TASK-260218-abc_design.md, type=precondition, content=\"...\", description=\"Architecture design\")'\n20|task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=reports/TASK-260218-abc_results.md, type=outcome, content=\"...\", description=\"Research findings\")'\n21|\n22|# Replace an existing resource\n23|task-board m 'update_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=reports/TASK-260218-abc_results.md, type=outcome, content=\"revised findings\", description=\"Research findings v2\")'\n24|task-board resource update TASK-260218-abc ./TASK-260218-abc_results.md --name reports/TASK-260218-abc_results.md --type outcome\n25|\n26|# Adopt an existing orphaned local payload without rewriting it\n27|task-board resource adopt TASK-260218-abc revisions/2/TASK-260218-abc_results.md --type outcome --description \"Recovered result\"\n28|\n29|# Delete a resource (destructive — requires --confirm)\n30|task-board m --confirm 'delete_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=artifacts/obsolete/TASK-260218-abc_design.md)'\n31|task-board resource delete TASK-260218-abc artifacts/obsolete/TASK-260218-abc_design.md --confirm\n32|\n33|# View resources on an element\n34|task-board q --format compact 'get(TASK-260218-abc) { preconditionResources outcomeResources }'\n35|```\n36|\n37|## Element-Owned Storage\n38|\n39|Resources from different tasks are not stored in one shared file pile. Each\n40|element gets its own directory, and every resource attached to that element is\n41|stored below it:\n42|\n43|```\n44|.task-board/.resources/\n45|├── TASK-260203-g7h8i9/\n46|│   ├── findings/\n47|│   │   └── investigation.md\n48|│   ├── artifacts/\n49|│   │   └── run-1/\n50|│   │       └── output.json\n51|│   ├── reports/\n52|│   │   └── TASK-260203-g7h8i9_results.md\n53|│   └── revisions/\n54|│       └── 2/\n55|│           └── review.md\n56|└── STORY-260203-d4e5f6/\n57|    └── research.md         # outcome\n58|```\n59|\n60|The resource `name` is a safe forward-slash-relative path. Agents may choose\n61|the hierarchy that fits the artifact and nest it further as needed. Every\n62|segment must be non-empty printable UTF-8 and must not be `.`, `..`, an\n63|absolute/drive-qualified path, or contain a backslash. Raw forward slashes are\n64|the only hierarchy delimiter; malformed URL escapes and encoded or repeatedly\n65|encoded separators/traversal are rejected. Attach related files to the same\n66|owning element; do not invent a generic board-wide resource task or write\n67|payloads into `.task-board/.resources/` manually.\n68|\n69|Directories are structural nodes, not payloads. Resource CRUD, validation, and\n70|handoff evidence recognize regular files only; a directory named like a report\n71|cannot be adopted or used to satisfy outcome evidence.\n72|\n73|Local and board-server filesystem element deletion is journaled and\n74|crash-recoverable. Direct resource CRUD first resolves any pending staged\n75|element delete under the board mutation lock. MinIO element/subtree deletion\n76|currently fails before mutation with the typed\n77|`ErrAtomicResourceDeleteUnsupported` capability error; ordinary resource CRUD\n78|remains available.\n79|\n80|References are tracked in `progress.md` as markdown links:\n81|```markdown\n82|## Precondition Resources\n83|- [specs/auth/design.md](board-resource://TASK-260203-g7h8i9/precondition/specs/auth/design.md) — Architecture design\n84|\n85|## Outcome Resources\n86|- [reports/TASK-260203-g7h8i9_results.md](board-resource://TASK-260203-g7h8i9/outcome/reports/TASK-260203-g7h8i9_results.md) — Research findings\n87|```\n88|\n89|## Spawn Integration\n90|\n91|Precondition resources are automatically injected into agent prompts by `task-board spawn`. Full prompts preserve normal text inlining. Lite prompts use the resolved `agent_context.prompt.preconditions` policy: by default, text below `inline_bytes` is rendered inline, while larger text and binary resources are written read-only under `.temp/resources/` and represented by their name, description, byte count, SHA-256 digest, and local path. This means:\n92|\n93|1. Attach instructions/specs as precondition resources to a task\n94|2. Run `task-board spawn TASK-XX --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max` — agent gets everything automatically\n95|3. Agent saves results via `task-board m 'add_resource(..., type=outcome)'` on first write, then `update_resource(...)` for revisions\n96|\n97|## Best Practices\n98|\n99|- **Use preconditions for agent instructions** — attach design docs, specs, or step-by-step instructions before spawning\n100|- **Use outcomes for work products** — research findings, analysis, implementation notes\n101|- **Attach to the owning element** — pass the Task, Bug, Story, or Epic ID that owns the artifact; the storage layer groups its payloads under that element directory automatically\n102|- **Use explicit create/update/delete** — `add_resource` / `resource add` must not silently overwrite; use `update_resource` / `resource update` when replacing an existing payload\n103|- **Use adopt only for local repair** — `resource adopt` registers bytes already stored at `.resources/<elementID>/<relative-resource-path>` without rewriting them; a missing payload returns resource-not-found and an existing declaration returns resource-exists\n104|- **Choose a useful hierarchy inside the owning element** — `findings/`, `artifacts/`, `reports/`, and `revisions/` are conventions, not a fixed schema; nest further when it makes the handoff easier to navigate\n105|- **Use safe relative resource paths** — `/` separates validated path segments; empty, dot/traversal, absolute/drive-qualified, backslash, control-character, malformed escape, and encoded/repeatedly encoded separator or traversal forms are rejected in local and remote storage\n106|- **Attach files, not folders** — directories only organize resource files and never satisfy resource existence or handoff evidence\n107|- **Always use board commands** — never create/edit resource files or progress.md resource sections manually\n108|- **Name handoff evidence with task scope** — keep the task ID in the resource path, for example `reports/TASK-260218-abc_architecture-design.md`, so `task-board handoff` can recognize it\n109|- **Add descriptions** — the `description=` param adds a one-line description shown in spawn prompts\n110|\n111|---\n112|\n113|# Bugs\n114|\n115|Bugs are elements of the board, living inside stories alongside tasks.\n116|\n117|```bash\n118|# Create bug\n119|task-board m 'create(type=bug, parent=STORY-260218-abc, name=crash-on-start, description=\"App crashes when starting recording\")'\n120|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
